Condition : 6 - Prior to the commencement of the development, including any demolition works, an Ecological Management Plan (EMP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The EMP shall incorporate:
i.details of measures to protect breeding birds, nests and eggs from mortality/damage, injury and disturbance, including avoidance by timing and/or appropriate supervision, and a commitment to alert the LPA in the event of unexpected sightings of protected species during construction (including details of construction protocol in such a scenario);
ii.specific provisions for the protection and enhancement of the Grey Wagtail habitat identified at the site;
iii.details of the ecological clerk of works supervision to be put in place to monitor the clearance of vegetation to ensure no impact on undiscovered or other unexpected faunal encounters;
iv.an ecological lighting plan / strategy showing how lighting on site would be designed to avoid harm to existing and future ecology on site (e.g. light intensity and hours of use);
v.finalised details of ecological enhancement, including biodiversity net gains (plus supporting biometric calculations/ area habitat summary) and urban greening factor;
vi.details of how the enhancement measures will be monitored, managed and maintained, including the long-term design objectives, management responsibilities and maintenance schedules;
vii.details on the location and type (including specifications) of bird boxes and other appropriate ecological enhancements (e.g. nest boxes / bricks / cups for house martins and swifts etc.; bat boxes; insect blocks; reptile log piles; hedgehog houses etc.), in addition to maintenance provisions and a commitment that any data collected is to be shared with the Council.
viii.species surveys within and around the site to demonstrate ecological enhancements. The development shall then be carried out in strict accordance with the approved details.
Reason: In the interest of mainta

Condition : 28 - Notwithstanding the submitted details, before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, a finalised Parking Management Plan shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Plan shall include the following:
(i) a commitment to review and fully justify the number of parking spaces once the end-user is known;
(ii) details of measures to restrict parking to the 10 designated bays shown on the approved plans only, including how this provision will be operated and how parking outside the marked bays (e.g. elsewhere on site or at the neighbouring site) will be prohibited and enforced;
(iii) a commitment to convert passive EV bays to active and to provide additional Blue Badge bays when demand requires;
(iv) details of the operation of any gates or barriers;
(v) details of how parking will be monitored and managed during shift changeovers;
(vi) measures to ensure that all prospective occupiers are informed of the Parking Management Plan. 
The parking and circulation areas and access road(s) shall thereafter be managed in compliance with the approved Parking Management Plan, unless the prior written approval of the Local Planning Authority is obtained to secure any variation.
Reason: To promote sustainable modes of transport and ensure that the scheme does not give rise to highway safety concerns.
